File scripts/data/effect-backfill.json — add one row (the same shape as the shipped `acute-vision` / `acute-scent` whileActive rows):
{
  "category": "feats",
  "id": "nocturnal-senses",
  "field": "whileActive",
  "value": [
    {
      "state": "rage",
      "conditionalSenses": [
        { "ifPresent": "low-light-vision", "upgraded": { "name": "darkvision", "acuity": "precise" } },
        { "ifPresent": "scent", "upgraded": { "name": "scent", "range": 60, "acuity": "imprecise" } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
No `base` on either entry — that is the point of the type change above, and it reproduces their empty `falseOperations`. `ifPresent` spelling: the loop's `norm()` at derive.ts:2554 strips a trailing `-vision` and folds whitespace/underscores to hyphens, so "low-light-vision" matches an ancestry `vision` of `low-light-vision` and their `"low-light vision"` alike; `scent` matches an ancestry/feat scent grant. `upgraded` (not `increaseRangeBy`) for the scent branch because the print says "increases TO 60 feet", an absolute, and `addSense` (derive.ts:2421) keeps the better range so an existing scent 30 is raised and a scent 60 is left alone. Note also that this makes the pre-existing NOT_A_SCALAR settle for SENSES_IMPRECISE at scripts/wg-values.mjs:144 ("covered by `senses` / `conditionalSenses`") true for this record for the first time; no registry edit needed.

