COLLATERAL, found while reading print — not a WG difference (their ops encode no activation cost and no frequency), so flagging rather than asserting. Our record says `activationCost: {type:"actions", value:1}` and `frequency: {max:1, per:"day"}`, while the record's OWN description text three lines below reads "**Activate** ⟨2⟩ envision, Interact" and prints no Frequency at all. The rows would be:
{"category":"items","id":"aeon-stone-western-star","field":"activationCost","value":{"type":"actions","value":2}}
{"category":"items","id":"aeon-stone-western-star","field":"frequency","value":null}
BUT this is family-wide, not per-record: 20 of the 21 legacy aeon stones in core.json carry the identical blanket {1 action, 1/day}, and spot-checking print shows Pale Lavender Ellipsoid is a Reaction (freq once/day), Agate Ellipsoid a Reaction with NO frequency, Rainbow Prism Two Actions (freq three/day), Dusty Rose Prism no Activate line at all. It is an import default in the base generator, not authored per stone. Recommend it be fixed for the whole aeon-stone family by the script that owns the item-activation lane rather than by one overlay row here.
